From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 07:25:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2: pass the colours and the HDR10 metadata to the encoder
 device

The encoder interface had no colour aspects, so a client's colour range,
primaries, transfer and matrix never reached the device or the stream.
Add the colour aspects of the frames and the VUI colour aspects of the
stream, as the software encoders do. The encoder sets the V4L2 colorimetry
of the raw frames from them, in the format of the raw queue, which is
where the device reads it.

Main 10 encodes 10-bit frames, which the device must take as P010 for the
profile to make sense. The device query leaves Main 10 out of the profiles
when the device lists no P010 input; it lists the raw formats for the HEVC
coded format, since a device lists them per coded format. The interface
offers the P010 pixel format with that profile, which the framework lists as
a colour format, and the encoder takes P010 frames for the profile. P010 is
one buffer that holds both colour planes, so V4L2 names it with the fourcc
of a single buffer, the CbCr plane starts after the Y plane at the same
stride, and its element is a pair of 16-bit samples. A device that lists the
HDR10 mastering display and content light level controls on top of that
offers the HDR static info parameter, which is the sign for the framework to
list the HDR10 profile, and the encoder sets the two compound controls from
it in the units of the SEI messages.
